-- o 5 r 1(4): duty decision function in layer 1: `o 5 r 1(4) the party may reject an offer of amicable resolution` (N2: the flat negative gives JUST FALSE and the SHANT is derived from it)
DECLARE `o 5 r 1(4) the party` IS ONE OF `o 5 r 1(4) party to the proceedings`
DECLARE `o 5 r 1(4) the act` IS ONE OF `o 5 r 1(4) reject an offer of amicable resolution` HAS `with reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:476 | (4) A party to any proceedings must not reject an offer of amicable resolution unless the party has reasonable grounds to do so.
@ref O 5 r 1(4) (src:476)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 5 r 1(4) the party` `o 5 r 1(4) the act`
`o 5 r 1(4) the duty` MEANS
    PARTY `o 5 r 1(4) party to the proceedings`
    SHANT `o 5 r 1(4) reject an offer of amicable resolution` grounds PROVIDED (NOT grounds)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the party rejected an offer of amicable resolution without reasonable grounds"

-- rejects the offer on day 3 with reasonable grounds: the prohibition does not bite; expected the prohibition still printed back (no breach)
